{% extends 'layouts/page.njk' %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">About Design help</h1>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        Design help supports the Defra design team in using the <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ frameworkUrl }}">GDaD (Government Digital and Data) framework</a> for pay. The framework sets the skills each design role needs and links your capability level to your pay.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What it&rsquo;s for</h2>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Designers record evidence against each GDaD skill for their role, see their scores and capability level, and build new evidence for their next review.</li>
        <li>Line managers can see the evidence of the people they manage.</li>
        <li>The Head of Design scores evidence, tells people their results, keeps a record of earlier evidence and scores, and exports scores for the GDaD pay and reward team.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Who can see your evidence</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Only you, your line manager and the Head of Design can see your evidence and scores. Other admins cannot see them.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Your scores, but not your evidence, are shared with the GDaD pay and reward team.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">The GDaD year</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        The GDaD year starts on 1 July. Evidence is usually scored at the end of September, and any pay change is backdated to 1 July.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Between reviews you build new evidence for the next one. New starters are assessed when they join.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How Design help has changed</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Design help started as a way for designers to find and offer help to each other, such as design critiques, design tooling and coaching. This was after the team moved to resource managers handling line management. That directory is still available under Find help.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        As the team&rsquo;s needs became clearer, it grew into the place where we record and score GDaD evidence. This is now its main purpose.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Feedback</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        If something does not work, <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" href="{{ feedbackLinkHref }}">give feedback about this service</a> (about 2 minutes) or speak to your line manager.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How it has been built</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        There is a longer account of the technology, how the service is hosted, use of assistive AI in development, accessibility choices, and what we have (and have not) assured for security.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
        <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" href="/how-it-has-been-built">Read more about how design help was built</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
